<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  VM live NEGATIVE test: the form_input dialog pointed at a REAL Nextcloud, where it must fail.

  This is the other half of the pair whose positive half is vm-nextcloud-form.xml. The two dialogs are
  not interchangeable, and this fixture is what keeps that from being an assumption:

    vm-nextcloud-form.xml   <response attribute="data-requesttoken">   against Nextcloud  -> works
    this fixture             <response form_input="requesttoken">       against Nextcloud  -> must not

  Nextcloud's password dialog is script-rendered. The page carries no <form>, and its hidden inputs are
  'initial-state-*' blobs keyed by 'id' with no 'name' at all, so a scan that matches name= finds
  nothing however the rest of the dialog is spelled. The CSRF token is on a <head> attribute instead.

  The GET is aimed at /authenticate/showshare, which answers 200, precisely so the failure comes from
  the CAPTURE and not from a status: aimed at /s/<token> the step would fail on the 303 first, which
  would prove nothing about form_input.

  What SHOULD appear in the log, and what makes this test meaningful rather than merely red:

      Form input scan: 'requesttoken' not found in the response body
      REST capture 'rt' found no value in the response and has no 'default'; the dialog cannot
      continue. Check that the server still serves this value.

  That is the S5 fail-closed rule doing its job: the login is NOT attempted with an empty token, and
  the message names the capture that could not be resolved. A silent empty POST would surface later as
  an opaque 403 from the server, which is the failure mode this design exists to avoid.

  Token, password and paths match the share setup_nextcloud.sh provisions, and /index.php is there for
  the same reason as in vm-nextcloud-form.xml: this bench does not serve pretty URLs.
-->
<dfir-orc>
    <upload method="REST" server="%ORC_UPLOAD_SERVER%"
            https_security="tls1.3, tls1.2" operation="copy"
            server_cert_pin="">

        <rest http_method="GET" path="/index.php/s/orcvmshare00000/authenticate/showshare" session="once">
            <response form_input="requesttoken" name="rt"/>
            <response form_input="sharingToken" name="st"/>
            <response form_input="sharingType"  name="sy"/>
        </rest>

        <rest http_method="POST" path="/index.php/s/orcvmshare00000/authenticate/showshare"
              session="once" accept_status="302,303">
            <form field="password"     value="orc-share-not-a-secret"/>
            <form field="requestToken" value="{rt}"/>
            <form field="sharingToken" value="{st}"/>
            <form field="sharingType"  value="{sy}"/>
        </rest>

        <rest http_method="PUT"
              path="/public.php/dav/files/orcvmshare00000/{upload.filename}"
              body="{upload.local_path}"/>

    </upload>
</dfir-orc>
